{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530550-question-about-eightfold-yin-mantle-yin-prana-4","id":1530550,"title":"Question about Eightfold Yin Mantle (Yin Prana 4)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-11T08:04:36-08:00","id":1530550,"title":"Question about Eightfold Yin Mantle (Yin Prana 4)","content":"Hello there!<br /> I was wondering how do you approach Yin Prana 4 in your chronicle (we are running KOTE in conjunction with V20/W20/M20/WTO20/C20).<br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/Vyb5bOj.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> The problem lies in the fact that the book doesn't specify anything about duration, nor sets limits to the amount of Yin Chi the Cathayan can spend while conjuring the item.<br /> That means nothing would stop a seasoned Bone Flower from spending all 10 Yin Chi points to conjure a weapon that deals Strength + 9/Aggravated, which is not only unbreakable, but lasts indefinitely...<br /> <br /> Now you might be thinking, &quot;well, just house rule that these conjured items last for a scene&quot;. Unfortunately, that would turn the use of this power to conjure weapons almost useless.<br /> Any Kuei-jin (without even Yin Prana) can make a Katana out of Black Jade, and spend one Yin point to charge it. By doing that, you will not only deal Strength+3 (+4 when two-handed) / Aggravated, but also strip Gnosis/Pathos away when striking a spirit/hengeyokai/wraith.<br /> <br /> Making a similar Katana with Eightfold Yin Mantle would cost somewhere between 4 to 5 Yin Chi points... and if it lasts for a scene I see no point to conjure it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25177-lirbo","name":"Lirbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T09:04:47-08:00","id":1530552,"title":"","content":"Actually this is easy to answer<br /> <br /> &quot;Spending Chi&quot; - P.139<br /> Lesser Kuei-jin may spend only one point of Chi per turn. However, if a character has a high rating in her Dharma, she may spend more than one point per turn.<br /> See p. 54 for more information.<br /> <br /> Dharma lvl 4-5 - 2 Chi/turn<br /> Dharma level 6 - 3 Chi/turn<br /> Dharma level 7 - 4 Ci/turn<br /> Dharma level 8 - 6 Chi/turn<br /> Dharma level 9 - 8 chi/turn<br /> Dharma level 10 - ? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T09:10:09-08:00","id":1530553,"title":"","content":"Sorry I don't dare to edit<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lirbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530550-question-about-eightfold-yin-mantle-yin-prana-4#post1530550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any Kuei-jin (without even Yin Prana) can make a Katana out of Black Jade, and spend one Yin point to charge it.</div> </div> </div> </div>A katana worth of Black Jade is quite an amount mind you and aquireing that amount is probably the story of its own<br /> Jade is rare and precious<br /> Not that reaching <b>Yin Prana 4 </b>is easier... As with the Yang Prana, the Yin Prana is a complicated endeavor; a student may raise his level in this Discipline no higher than the lower of his Perception and Stamina ratings.<br /> <br /> So it is quite balanced if you asks me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T09:36:07-08:00","id":1530557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530550-question-about-eightfold-yin-mantle-yin-prana-4?p=1530552#post1530552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually this is easy to answer<br /> <br /> &quot;Spending Chi&quot; - P.139<br /> Lesser Kuei-jin may spend only one point of Chi per turn. However, if a character has a high rating in her Dharma, she may spend more than one point per turn.<br /> See p. 54 for more information.<br /> <br /> Dharma lvl 4-5 - 2 Chi/turn<br /> Dharma level 6 - 3 Chi/turn<br /> Dharma level 7 - 4 Ci/turn<br /> Dharma level 8 - 6 Chi/turn<br /> Dharma level 9 - 8 chi/turn<br /> Dharma level 10 - ?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hi, first of all thank you for answering!<br /> Taking the Chi/turn limit as limitation can definitely be an interesting option. But then I believe it creates another problem? If a Running Monkey is unable to spend more than 1 turn into the conjuration of an item, how would they be able to activate powers that require more than 1 Chi point?<br /> <br /> Example:<br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/SnYNP0r.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/SnYNP0r.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/SnYNP0r.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> Or you simply enable the Cathayan to exceed their Dharmic limits for such powers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25177-lirbo","user":"Lirbo","date":". 02-11-2024, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25177-lirbo","name":"Lirbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T09:51:02-08:00","id":1530558,"title":"","content":"The Chi/turn limitation actually doesn't limit how much you can pump into the power. You can charge up an open-ended power over successive turns. The downside to this is that you'll probably end up quite low on juice; there was also some potential that spirits might take offense at &quot;atomizing the local chi-scape&quot;, but that seems like it would take more power than you could muster at Dharma levels less than 6 or 7 unless you soaked up more chi than you could safely hold, which brings on the danger of making one of the Hungry Dead blow themselves up (a much more tangible danger than spirits not liking you when a lot of them probably already don't like you).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T09:55:47-08:00","id":1530559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lirbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530550-question-about-eightfold-yin-mantle-yin-prana-4#post1530550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello there!<br /> I was wondering how do you approach Yin Prana 4 in your chronicle (we are running KOTE in conjunction with V20/W20/M20/WTO20/C20).<br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/Vyb5bOj.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> The problem lies in the fact that the book doesn't specify anything about duration, nor sets limits to the amount of Yin Chi the Cathayan can spend while conjuring the item.<br /> That means nothing would stop a seasoned Bone Flower from spending all 10 Yin Chi points to conjure a weapon that deals Strength + 9/Aggravated, which is not only unbreakable, but lasts indefinitely...<br /> <br /> Now you might be thinking, &quot;well, just house rule that these conjured items last for a scene&quot;. Unfortunately, that would turn the use of this power to conjure weapons almost useless.<br /> Any Kuei-jin (without even Yin Prana) can make a Katana out of Black Jade, and spend one Yin point to charge it. By doing that, you will not only deal Strength+3 (+4 when two-handed) / Aggravated, but also strip Gnosis/Pathos away when striking a spirit/hengeyokai/wraith.<br /> <br /> Making a similar Katana with Eightfold Yin Mantle would cost somewhere between 4 to 5 Yin Chi points... and if it lasts for a scene I see no point to conjure it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see the problem. 10 Yin Chi is not little, and from how I read the power, Strength 5+ is enough to break it (can't remember what rolls it takes, but if it's something like roll Strength on difficulty 8 or less, 5 dice is enough to succeed on average). Swords in VDA20 take Strength 5 (but without needing to roll) to be bent. So it's not really an unbreakable sword, even if it does a ton of damage. It looks and feels weird too, which will require careful handling to avoid attracting unwanted attention. And it's a 4th level power requiring at least Perception and Stamina 4, according to what Shadeprowler said. It's alright for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T09:58:03-08:00","id":1530561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lirbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530550-question-about-eightfold-yin-mantle-yin-prana-4?p=1530557#post1530557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Taking the Chi/turn limit as limitation can definitely be an interesting option. But then I believe it creates another problem? If a Running Monkey is unable to spend more than 1 turn into the conjuration of an item, how would they be able to activate powers that require more than 1 Chi point?</div> </div> </div> </div>Either that - I mean for a level 4 power having at least 4 point of Dharma not that farfatched in a game where dharmic advance is a mayor focus - or let them spend the required chi to activate the power but any aditional point to be tied to the spending/turn limit in my humble opinion<br /> <br /> And what Saur Ops Specialist wrote is also true<br /> Spending high amount of chi is quite dangerous and draining such ambient chi from the area could result in a bunch very angry yokai wanting to talk with you how your ancestors are dissapointed by your behaviour so to speak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T10:02:16-08:00","id":1530562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530550-question-about-eightfold-yin-mantle-yin-prana-4?p=1530559#post1530559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see the problem. 10 Yin Chi is not little, and from how I read the power, Strength 5+ is enough to break it (can't remember what rolls it takes, but if it's something like roll Strength on difficulty 8 or less, 5 dice is enough to succeed on average). Swords in VDA20 take Strength 5 (but without needing to roll) to be bent. So it's not really an unbreakable sword, even if it does a ton of damage. It looks and feels weird too, which will require careful handling to avoid attracting unwanted attention. And it's a 4th level power requiring at least Perception and Stamina 4, according to what Shadeprowler said. It's alright for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The power makes it seem way harder than this. Though, since the KotE Disciplines are left out in the cold and won't be getting any further revisions beyond the slap-dash measure all the way back in the Revised Storyteller's Handbook, we'll likely never get hard numbers on how durable the materialized objects were actually intended to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T10:32:21-08:00","id":1530564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530550-question-about-eightfold-yin-mantle-yin-prana-4?p=1530558#post1530558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Chi/turn limitation actually doesn't limit how much you can pump into the power. You can charge up an open-ended power over successive turns. The downside to this is that you'll probably end up quite low on juice; there was also some potential that spirits might take offense at &quot;atomizing the local chi-scape&quot;, but that seems like it would take more power than you could muster at Dharma levels less than 6 or 7 unless you soaked up more chi than you could safely hold, which brings on the danger of making one of the Hungry Dead blow themselves up (a much more tangible danger than spirits not liking you when a lot of them probably already don't like you).</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, it certainly means you indulged more than you can possibly hold, though the risk for doing something that like that is very minimal if you &quot;charge yourself up&quot; by feeding to the maximum (10 Chi Points if you are below Dharma 6), and then spend all of it right after as you conjure a sword. Chi explosion only happens when you botch a roll that requires Chi expenditure while having more Chi than you can hold. This power doesn't require any roll, and even if it did, a Willpower expenditure would have secured the conjuration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530550-question-about-eightfold-yin-mantle-yin-prana-4?p=1530559#post1530559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see the problem. 10 Yin Chi is not little, and from how I read the power, Strength 5+ is enough to break it (can't remember what rolls it takes, but if it's something like roll Strength on difficulty 8 or less, 5 dice is enough to succeed on average). Swords in VDA20 take Strength 5 (but without needing to roll) to be bent. So it's not really an unbreakable sword, even if it does a ton of damage. It looks and feels weird too, which will require careful handling to avoid attracting unwanted attention. And it's a 4th level power requiring at least Perception and Stamina 4, according to what Shadeprowler said. It's alright for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> I mean yeah sure it's breakable, but I'm afraid that's the least of my concerns regarding this power x)<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------------<br /> <br /> Regardless, I don't really see how it should anger local spirits if the Chi that was used is not ambient-chi, but stolen through blood.<br /> I think it's a real menace, though. The possibility of creating such weapons is essentially making this power abhorrently strong.<br /> <br /> <br /> In my chronicle I kind of merged it with the rules of Path of Conjuring (V20), though I am not a fan of deviating from the official books.<br /> <i>Objects conjured using the Eightfold Yin Mantle must be mundane and non-complex. Such objects last for the remainder of the night, and crumble to dust upon sunlight exposure. Conjured weapons operate at difficulty 6, and inflict Strength +0/Aggravated damage, with the option to increase damage at the expense of additional Yin Chi points. Alternatively, the Cathayan can conjure weapons with default stats from the Official Arsenal by expending one Yin Chi, plus an extra Yin Chi per damage die or reduced difficulty. For example, conjuring a dagger (difficulty 4, Strength +1) would require a total of 4 Yin Chi. Eightfold Yin Prana users may never conjure anything that requires more Yin Chi points than their Yin Prana rating. Finally, objects can be made permanent by spending a Willpower point and two additional Yin Chi points.</i><br /> <br /> Opinions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25177-lirbo","name":"Lirbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T13:09:40-08:00","id":1530582,"title":"","content":"It's going a bit too far in the other direction, I think, to make a power struggle and strain to make a long knife. Also, the term &quot;Cathayan&quot; was rarely used by the end of the line, in favor of Gui Ren and other terms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T15:05:14-08:00","id":1530589,"title":"","content":"Just have it last until the sun rises.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}